IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `esl-levy`
IMPORT `esl-qa`

-- Emergency Services Levy Act 2002 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (esl-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role
-- and every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the role it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the answer
-- must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error. Each
-- question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with FALSE (the situation does not hold) and every
-- later input ASSUMEd: the answer must be `does not arise for you`. Every situation input is a BOOLEAN, so the trap of
-- graffiti finding 31 cannot hide a read of it.
--
-- For the owner (the baseline's seat), each case is asserted twice: once against a value worked by hand from the text
-- (most taken from the baseline's own cases, esl-cases-levy.l4, and the life c055), and once against the baseline
-- export's own answer on the same facts, carried into the layer's answer type. For the tenant or occupier the values
-- are worked by hand from the text. The rates in the determinations are illustrative, as in the baseline.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked land` IS A `My land for the levy year`
ASSUME `an unasked determination` IS A `The determination for my land`
ASSUME `an unasked interest` IS A `My interest in the land`
ASSUME `an unasked assessor` IS A `Who assessed my levy`

`as the owner` MEANS `I own land in Western Australia`
`as the tenant or occupier` MEANS `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns`

-- The land and determinations of the baseline's cases (esl-cases-levy.l4), restated here: a case file is not imported.
`c055: Chloe and Liam's Byford house, 2029/30` MEANS `My land for the levy year` WITH
    `is located in an ESL category area` IS TRUE
    `is of a kind wholly exempt from the levy under the regulations` IS FALSE
    `another enactment purports to exempt me from it` IS FALSE
    `that enactment was passed after section 36E commenced` IS FALSE
    `that enactment expressly exempts me from the levy` IS FALSE

`land outside every ESL category area` MEANS `My land for the levy year` WITH
    `is located in an ESL category area` IS FALSE
    `is of a kind wholly exempt from the levy under the regulations` IS FALSE
    `another enactment purports to exempt me from it` IS FALSE
    `that enactment was passed after section 36E commenced` IS FALSE
    `that enactment expressly exempts me from the levy` IS FALSE

`land of a kind exempt under the regulations` MEANS `My land for the levy year` WITH
    `is located in an ESL category area` IS TRUE
    `is of a kind wholly exempt from the levy under the regulations` IS TRUE
    `another enactment purports to exempt me from it` IS FALSE
    `that enactment was passed after section 36E commenced` IS FALSE
    `that enactment expressly exempts me from the levy` IS FALSE

`land whose owner relies on an older Act exempting from all rates` MEANS `My land for the levy year` WITH
    `is located in an ESL category area` IS TRUE
    `is of a kind wholly exempt from the levy under the regulations` IS FALSE
    `another enactment purports to exempt me from it` IS TRUE
    `that enactment was passed after section 36E commenced` IS FALSE
    `that enactment expressly exempts me from the levy` IS FALSE

`land under a later Act expressly exempting its owner from the levy` MEANS `My land for the levy year` WITH
    `is located in an ESL category area` IS TRUE
    `is of a kind wholly exempt from the levy under the regulations` IS FALSE
    `another enactment purports to exempt me from it` IS TRUE
    `that enactment was passed after section 36E commenced` IS TRUE
    `that enactment expressly exempts me from the levy` IS TRUE

`land under a later Act exempting from all rates and taxes, not naming the levy` MEANS `My land for the levy year` WITH
    `is located in an ESL category area` IS TRUE
    `is of a kind wholly exempt from the levy under the regulations` IS FALSE
    `another enactment purports to exempt me from it` IS TRUE
    `that enactment was passed after section 36E commenced` IS TRUE
    `that enactment expressly exempts me from the levy` IS FALSE

`c055 assumed determination: 1.2 cents in the dollar, minimum 90, maximum 450` MEANS `The determination for my land` WITH
    `rate in the dollar of gross rental value` IS 0.012
    `a minimum is determined` IS TRUE
    `minimum levy` IS 90
    `a maximum is determined` IS TRUE
    `maximum levy` IS 450
    `the Minister determined the levy on my land on another basis` IS FALSE
    `the levy on that other basis` IS 0

`an assumed determination with no minimum or maximum` MEANS `The determination for my land` WITH
    `rate in the dollar of gross rental value` IS 0.012
    `a minimum is determined` IS FALSE
    `minimum levy` IS 0
    `a maximum is determined` IS FALSE
    `maximum levy` IS 0
    `the Minister determined the levy on my land on another basis` IS FALSE
    `the levy on that other basis` IS 0

`an assumed determination on another basis of 50, minimum 90` MEANS `The determination for my land` WITH
    `rate in the dollar of gross rental value` IS 0.012
    `a minimum is determined` IS TRUE
    `minimum levy` IS 90
    `a maximum is determined` IS TRUE
    `maximum levy` IS 450
    `the Minister determined the levy on my land on another basis` IS TRUE
    `the levy on that other basis` IS 50

§§ `For the land owner (the baseline's seat)`

-- Does the Emergency Services Levy Act itself fix my levy?
#ASSERT `Does the Emergency Services Levy Act itself fix my levy` `as the owner` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does the Emergency Services Levy Act itself fix my levy` `as the owner` EQUALS (`yes if` (`Does the Emergency Services Levy Act itself fix how much levy I pay`))
#ASSERT `Does the Emergency Services Levy Act itself fix my levy` `as the tenant or occupier` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- Does another law's exemption free me from the levy?
#ASSERT `Does another law's exemption free me from the levy` `as the owner` `land under a later Act expressly exempting its owner from the levy` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Does another law's exemption free me from the levy` `as the owner` `land under a later Act expressly exempting its owner from the levy` EQUALS (`yes if` (`Does another law exempt me from the levy` `land under a later Act expressly exempting its owner from the levy`))
-- s 36E: not express.
#ASSERT `Does another law's exemption free me from the levy` `as the owner` `land under a later Act exempting from all rates and taxes, not naming the levy` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does another law's exemption free me from the levy` `as the owner` `land under a later Act exempting from all rates and taxes, not naming the levy` EQUALS (`yes if` (`Does another law exempt me from the levy` `land under a later Act exempting from all rates and taxes, not naming the levy`))
-- s 36E: passed before it.
#ASSERT `Does another law's exemption free me from the levy` `as the owner` `land whose owner relies on an older Act exempting from all rates` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does another law's exemption free me from the levy` `as the owner` `land whose owner relies on an older Act exempting from all rates` EQUALS (`yes if` (`Does another law exempt me from the levy` `land whose owner relies on an older Act exempting from all rates`))
#ASSERT `Does another law's exemption free me from the levy` `as the tenant or occupier` `an unasked land` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

